diagnosis_text:
A thorough multi-layer investigation found no evidence of the reported intermittent route flapping. The lab's two FRR BGP routers (router1 AS 1, router2 AS 2) are currently in a fully Established session (`Connections established 1; dropped 0`) with both prefixes — 195.11.14.0/24 and 200.1.1.0/24 — correctly installed as active FIB routes on each router. The path pc1 → pc2 shows 0% packet loss.

To rule out an intermittent or past fault, every causal mechanism was directly tested: (1) no flap script, flap process, or cron job exists on either router; (2) carrier-change counters on the inter-router link (eth0) are at startup-only baseline with zero errors; (3) FRR logs on both routers have debug bgp keepalives and debug bgp updates enabled and contain only a single startup-transient reset followed by normal UPDATE exchange and regular keepalive traffic — no BGP WITHDRAW messages, no hold-timer expiry, no session drops appear anywhere in the 43-line log that covers the lab's entire lifetime; (4) no traffic-control shaping (tc/netem), no ACL rules, no MAC conflicts, and no addressing anomalies were found. The BGP configuration on both routers is standard, with no route dampening, no route-maps, and no conditional advertisement that could cause periodic withdrawal.

Root cause: No fault has been injected. The user's report of a route appearing and disappearing cannot be substantiated by any mechanism or historical trace in the live lab. The network is operating correctly.

Fix: No corrective action is required. The topology and BGP configuration are correct and stable.
=== END ===